<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n25850" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Lăpĭtha</span></b> , ae,
			com., and <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Lăpĭthes</span></b> , ae,
		m., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a
				Lapitha; plur.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Lăpĭthae</span></b> ,
			ārum, m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Λαπίθαι</span>, <i>the
				Lapithæ</i>, a rude tribe of mountaineers in
			Thessaly, about Olympus, who fought with the Centaurs at the wedding
			of Pirithŏüs, king of the Lapithæ,
				<i><span class="en">Ov.
				M. 12, 261</span></i>; <i><span class="en">536</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Hor. C. 1,
				18, 8</span></i>; <i><span class="en">2, 12, 5</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Cic. Pis.
				10, 22</span></i>.—<i>Gen. plur.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Lapithūm,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 7, 304</span></i>
			.—<i>Sing. gen.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Lapithae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					M. 12, 250</span></i>
			.—In <i>fem.</i> adjectively: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Lapithae genus heroinae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Prop.
					2, 2, 9</span></i>
			 (Müll. heroine); cf.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Lapithes eques,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Val.
					Fl. 5, 516</span></i>
			.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Lăpĭthaeus</span></b> , a, um, <i>adj., of</i> or <i>belonging to the
				Lapithæ, Lapithean</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">gens,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					M. 12, 530</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Lăpĭthēĭus</span></b> ,
				a, um, <i>adj., of the
				Lapithæ</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tecta,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					M. 12, 417</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">proelia,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					ib. 14, 670</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>C.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Lăpĭ-thōnĭus</span></b> ,
				a, um, <i>adj., of the
				Lapithæ</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nympha,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Stat.
					Th. 7, 297</span></i>
			.</div>
